//! The reference client's other locales, compiled from its vendored locale
//! trees.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/gen_locale.py` -- do not edit by hand. Run
//! `python tools/gen_locale.py` to regenerate, and `--check` to see whether this
//! file is what the tool emits. CI runs the check, so a vendored locale and this
//! table cannot drift apart.
//!
//! Each table is the reference's own sparse shape: `(index, template)` pairs,
//! sorted by index, where the index is a position in [`crate::text_gen::ALL`].
//! A key a locale does not carry is not in its table and falls back to English,
//! which is what the reference itself does (`fallbackLocale: 'en-US'` in
//! `app-frontend/src/i18n.config.ts`).
//!
//! The templates are the reference's own ICU, verbatim, including the arm
//! keywords `Intl.PluralRules` selects by: `zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`
//! and `other`, plus `=N` exact selectors. [`crate::locale`] fills one in.
//!
//! Every locale's keys are a subset of English's, which is why a table stores a
//! position rather than a key string: the key is already in the binary once, in
//! [`crate::text_gen::NAMES`]. The whole set is 89,177 entries, 2,700,238 bytes of
//! translated text.
//!
//! `ar-SA` is here and is **not** offered: the reference's own `LOCALES`
//! (`ui/src/composables/i18n.ts`) lists 32 codes with this one commented out as
//! RTL. It is compiled because the data exists and a measurement is worth more
//! than an omission; [`crate::locale::OFFERED`] is the list the language row
//! draws, and it is the reference's.

// A table is data: the entries are read by the setting that is in force, so
// most of them are unreachable from any one build of the shell. Refusing to
// compile them would make the tables depend on what the interface happens to
// draw, which is the drift this generator exists to prevent.
#![allow(dead_code)]

/// One locale's own strings.
///
/// `entries` is sorted by its first element, so a lookup is a binary search and
/// two locales' tables can be compared by walking them together.
pub struct Locale {
    /// The BCP-47 tag the reference's `LOCALES` spells it with.
    pub tag: &'static str,
    /// The primary language subtag, which selects the plural rule.
    pub language: &'static str,
    /// Whether the reference declares this locale `dir: 'rtl'`.
    pub rtl: bool,
    /// The position in [`crate::text_gen::ALL`] of the reference's own name
    /// for this language (`locale.<tag>`).
    ///
    /// Resolved here rather than at runtime because the lookup is a scan of
    /// 3,846 keys and the label is drawn for every offered language at once.
    /// It resolves for every one of the 32 offered codes today -- the English
    /// locale carries all 32 `locale.*` names -- so `None` is a guard for a
    /// tree that grows a code upstream has not named yet, and a name that is
    /// missing is answered with the tag rather than with one this launcher
    /// invents.
    pub label: Option<u16>,
    /// `(position in text_gen::ALL, this locale's template)`, sorted by position.
    pub entries: &'static [(u16, &'static str)],
}

/// Every locale tree on disk, by tag.
